{"call_id":"call_c0sns7VaEJ7DvEiVpvZe2dTA","process_id":"16694","turn_id":"019ca9a8-e09b-77f2-afac-9d05f44cb256","command":["/usr/bin/bash","-lc","kspec task get @01KJDQ1GZ --json"],"cwd":"/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"kspec task get @01KJDQ1GZ --json"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","stdout":"{\n  \"_ulid\": \"01KJDQ1GZVK77Y8CETXW2E56TG\",\n  \"slugs\": [],\n  \"title\": \"Web UI WebSocket connection unreliable - continually disconnects and reconnects. Needs investigation\",\n  \"type\": \"task\",\n  \"description\": \"Web UI WebSocket connection unreliable - continually disconnects and reconnects. Needs investigation into reconnection logic, heartbeat handling, or fallback to polling.\",\n  \"spec_ref\": \"@daemon-server\",\n  \"status\": \"needs_work\",\n  \"blocked_by\": [],\n  \"depends_on\": [],\n  \"context\": [],\n  \"priority\": 3,\n  \"tags\": [],\n  \"vcs_refs\": [],\n  \"session_id\": null,\n  \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T19:33:04.635Z\",\n  \"started_at\": \"2026-03-01T07:29:06.129Z\",\n  \"submitted_at\": \"2026-03-01T07:33:44.791Z\",\n  \"notes\": [\n    {\n      \"_ulid\": \"01KJDQC6EMCTTQFKDBQX9JCG55\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T19:38:54.292Z\",\n      \"author\": \"@claude\",\n      \"content\": \"ENRICHMENT — Standalone context for this task:\\n\\n**What**: The Web UI WebSocket connection continually disconnects and reconnects. The `WebSocketManager` in `packages/web-ui/src/lib/websocket/manager.ts` has exponential backoff reconnection (1s, 2s, 4s... max 30s, max 10 attempts), but users report seeing frequent disconnect/reconnect cycles in the console logs. This suggests either the server is closing connections, the keepalive/heartbeat mechanism is missing, or reconnection resets are happening incorrectly.\\n\\n**Where**:\\n- `packages/web-ui/src/lib/websocket/manager.ts` — The WebSocketManager class. Key areas:\\n  - `connect()` (line 150): creates WebSocket, sets up onopen/onmessage/onerror/onclose handlers\\n  - `scheduleReconnect()` (line 371): exponential backoff logic, max 10 attempts\\n  - `onclose` handler (line 183): triggers reconnect on any close event, even clean ones\\n  - No heartbeat/ping mechanism — if the server expects periodic pings, the connection may time out\\n- `packages/web-ui/src/lib/stores/connection.svelte.ts` — Connection store wrapping the manager\\n- Server-side WebSocket handler (in the daemon code) — check if it sends pings or has idle timeouts\\n\\n**How**: Investigation and fix areas:\\n1. **Add heartbeat/ping**: Implement a periodic ping from client to server (e.g., every 30s). Many WebSocket servers close idle connections after a timeout (often 60s). The client should send a ping command and expect a pong response.\\n2. **Don't reconnect on clean close**: The `onclose` handler (line 183) calls `scheduleReconnect()` unconditionally. If `event.code === 1000` (normal closure) and the client initiated it via `disconnect()`, skip reconnection. Currently `disconnect()` clears the timer, but there's a race if onclose fires after disconnect resets state.\\n3. **Check server-side idle timeout**: The daemon's WebSocket server may have an idle timeout that closes connections. Either increase it or implement heartbeat to keep alive.\\n4. **Consider connection health check**: After reconnecting, verify the connection is actually healthy (e.g., send a ping and wait for response) before transitioning to 'connected' state.\\n5. **Investigate MAX_RECONNECT_ATTEMPTS**: After 10 failed reconnects, the connection is abandoned permanently. Consider resetting the attempt counter after a successful connection that lasts longer than some threshold (e.g., 60s).\\n\\n**Done when**:\\n- WebSocket connection remains stable for extended periods without spurious disconnects\\n- Client sends periodic heartbeat/ping to prevent idle timeout\\n- Clean disconnects (code 1000 from client-initiated disconnect) don't trigger reconnection\\n- Console shows clean connection lifecycle without repeated disconnect/reconnect spam\\n- Connection lost indicator (10s threshold) only triggers for genuine server unavailability\\n- Tests cover: heartbeat keeps connection alive, clean close doesn't reconnect, reconnection works after genuine server restart\",\n      \"supersedes\": null,\n      \"superseded\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"_ulid\": \"01KJDQX0Y1T915X3M23D1VS9PP\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T19:48:05.698Z\",\n      \"author\": \"@claude\",\n      \"content\": \"Linked to @daemon-server spec (covers WebSocket protocol). Investigate and fix WebSocket reconnection reliability.\",\n      \"supersedes\": null,\n      \"superseded\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"_ulid\": \"01KJM2DPN621APMNNFFZCX3RN5\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-03-01T06:47:24.582Z\",\n      \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n      \"content\": \"Execution context:\\n- Background: Web UI websocket manager can enter reconnect churn due to stale onclose handlers from prior sockets and reconnect attempts after intentional disconnect.\\n- Scope: stabilize client connection lifecycle for intentional close and project-switch reconnects; add focused regression tests for stale-close and manual-disconnect behavior.\\n- Files: packages/web-ui/src/lib/websocket/manager.ts, tests/web-ui/websocket-manager.test.ts (new).\\n- Verification: run targeted vitest for websocket manager tests and relevant existing connection-related tests, then run full npm test before submit.\",\n      \"supersedes\": null,\n      \"superseded\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"_ulid\": \"01KJM2R4EQV8T6WJV405GP3XWQ\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-03-01T06:53:06.391Z\",\n      \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n      \"content\": \"Implemented WebSocket reconnect-stability fix in packages/web-ui/src/lib/websocket/manager.ts and added regression tests in tests/websocket-manager.test.ts.\\n\\nWhat changed:\\n- Added stale-socket guards in connect() event handlers so late events from old sockets are ignored and cannot null out the active connection.\\n- Added intentionalDisconnect tracking so manual disconnects do not schedule reconnect attempts.\\n- Updated disconnect() to detach current socket reference before close, preventing close-handler races with new connections.\\n- Added regression tests for:\\n  1) old-socket close after project switch does not disrupt active socket,\\n  2) intentional disconnect does not auto-reconnect,\\n  3) unexpected disconnect still triggers reconnect.\\n\\nVerification:\\n- npx vitest run tests/websocket-manager.test.ts (3 passed)\\n- npm test (fails on pre-existing baseline issues unrelated to this change):\\n  - tests/cli-serve.test.ts \\\"should show No projects registered when no projects exist\\\"\\n  - tests/cli/session-note-limit.test.ts timeout failures (2 cases)\\n- kspec validate (pre-existing project-wide schema/reference/alignment/completeness issues)\",\n      \"supersedes\": null,\n      \"superseded\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"_ulid\": \"01KJM2TCM0Y1NCBBZ9JZTKW183\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-03-01T06:54:20.288Z\",\n      \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n      \"content\": \"Submitted for review in PR #622: https://github.com/kynetic-ai/kynetic-spec/pull/622 (branch fix/web-ui-websocket-reconnect-race, commit 155276ca9). Implemented WebSocketManager stale-close race guard and intentional-disconnect reconnect suppression with regression coverage in tests/websocket-manager.test.ts. Verification: npx vitest run tests/websocket-manager.test.ts (3 passed). Full npm test and kspec validate still show pre-existing unrelated baseline failures/issues (cli-serve no-projects assertion, session-note-limit timeouts, existing validate schema/reference/alignment/completeness warnings/errors).\",\n      \"supersedes\": null,\n      \"superseded\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"_ulid\": \"01KJM385VE2C92BYG0GM4HK06T\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-03-01T07:01:52.110Z\",\n      \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n      \"content\": \"[FIX_CYCLE: 1] Review findings: MUST-FIX: PR #622 failed regression gate. npm test reports 3 failures (tests/cli-serve.test.ts foreground startup assertion; tests/cli/session-note-limit.test.ts two timeout failures). Review posted with inline comment; do not merge until full suite is green.\",\n      \"supersedes\": null,\n      \"superseded\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"_ulid\": \"01KJM52BE1CPS3RB3YKACD24BJ\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-03-01T07:33:38.369Z\",\n      \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n      \"content\": \"[FIX_CYCLE: 2] Rebased branch fix/web-ui-websocket-reconnect-race onto origin/main after PR #621 merged regression-flake fixes. Verified full suite on rebased head: npm test => 163 files passed, 3620 tests passed, 0 failed (3 skipped). No functional changes to websocket fix; update is to clear regression gate with current base.\",\n      \"supersedes\": null,\n      \"superseded\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"_ulid\": \"01KJM53KANY59NF9XDMGZ01TXT\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-03-01T07:34:19.221Z\",\n      \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n      \"content\": \"[FIX_CYCLE: 2] Force-pushed rebased head d0de668 to PR #622 and resolved prior MUST-FIX review thread after confirming full-suite pass. Re-ran check-unresolved-comments workflow to refresh status on the resolved thread.\",\n      \"supersedes\": null,\n      \"superseded\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"_ulid\": \"01KJMTH46XE9XKDEYD1YBBK6D4\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-03-01T13:48:42.590Z\",\n      \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n      \"content\": \"[FIX_CYCLE: 4] Review findings: MUST-FIX: PR #622 fails regression gate on current head d0de668 (CI test shard 2/3). New test tests/websocket-manager.test.ts triggers ReferenceError: crypto is not defined when subscribe() calls crypto.randomUUID(). Address CI compatibility and re-submit for review.\",\n      \"supersedes\": null,\n      \"superseded\": false\n    }\n  ],\n  \"todos\": [],\n  \"automation\": \"eligible\",\n  \"_sourceFile\": \"/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\",\n  \"inherited_traits\": [\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"@trait-json-output\",\n      \"title\": \"JSON Output Mode\",\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-1\",\n          \"given\": \"command supports JSON mode\",\n          \"when\": \"--json flag is provided\",\n          \"then\": \"output is valid JSON with no ANSI color codes\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-2\",\n          \"given\": \"JSON mode is active\",\n          \"when\": \"command completes successfully\",\n          \"then\": \"output includes all data available in human-readable mode\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-3\",\n          \"given\": \"JSON mode is active\",\n          \"when\": \"command encounters an error\",\n          \"then\": \"error is returned as JSON object with error field\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-4\",\n          \"given\": \"JSON output contains references\",\n          \"when\": \"output is generated\",\n          \"then\": \"references use @ prefix consistently\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-5\",\n          \"given\": \"JSON output contains timestamps\",\n          \"when\": \"output is generated\",\n          \"then\": \"timestamps use ISO 8601 format\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-6\",\n          \"given\": \"command supports --json\",\n          \"when\": \"used with other formatting flags\",\n          \"then\": \"--json takes precedence over other format options\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"@trait-error-guidance\",\n      \"title\": \"Error Messages with Recovery Guidance\",\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-1\",\n          \"given\": \"command encounters error\",\n          \"when\": \"error message is shown\",\n          \"then\": \"includes description of what went wrong\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-2\",\n          \"given\": \"command encounters error\",\n          \"when\": \"error message is shown\",\n          \"then\": \"includes suggested action to resolve\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-3\",\n          \"given\": \"reference not found\",\n          \"when\": \"error is shown\",\n          \"then\": \"suggests checking ref with kspec search or kspec <type> list\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-4\",\n          \"given\": \"invalid state transition\",\n          \"when\": \"error is shown\",\n          \"then\": \"indicates current state and valid next states\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-5\",\n          \"given\": \"validation error\",\n          \"when\": \"error is shown\",\n          \"then\": \"indicates which field/value failed validation\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-6\",\n          \"given\": \"error in JSON mode\",\n          \"when\": \"--json is active\",\n          \"then\": \"guidance included in structured error object\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"@trait-shadow-commit\",\n      \"title\": \"Shadow Branch Auto-Commit\",\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-1\",\n          \"given\": \"command modifies state in shadow worktree\",\n          \"when\": \"save operation completes successfully\",\n          \"then\": \"git commit is created in shadow branch with semantic message\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-2\",\n          \"given\": \"shadow commit is created\",\n          \"when\": \"commit message is generated\",\n          \"then\": \"message follows pattern operation-colon-ref-short with optional detail\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-3\",\n          \"given\": \"shadow commit is created\",\n          \"when\": \"item reference is available\",\n          \"then\": \"commit message includes ULID prefix (8 chars) or primary slug\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-4\",\n          \"given\": \"shadow is not configured (no worktree)\",\n          \"when\": \"command that would normally commit runs\",\n          \"then\": \"command completes successfully without attempting git operations\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-5\",\n          \"given\": \"save operation fails\",\n          \"when\": \"validation or IO error occurs\",\n          \"then\": \"no commit is attempted and error is returned\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-6\",\n          \"given\": \"shadow has remote configured\",\n          \"when\": \"commit succeeds\",\n          \"then\": \"push is attempted in fire-and-forget mode (failure doesn't block command)\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-7\",\n          \"given\": \"commit or push fails\",\n          \"when\": \"save succeeded but git operation failed\",\n          \"then\": \"command succeeds but outputs warning about sync state\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-8\",\n          \"given\": \"command performs multiple related saves\",\n          \"when\": \"all saves complete successfully\",\n          \"then\": \"single atomic commit covers all changes\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"@trait-localhost-security\",\n      \"title\": \"Localhost-Only Security\",\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-1\",\n          \"given\": \"server is starting\",\n          \"when\": \"binding to network interface\",\n          \"then\": \"only accepts connections from 127.0.0.1 and ::1 (IPv6 localhost)\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-2\",\n          \"given\": \"connection attempt from non-localhost\",\n          \"when\": \"request received\",\n          \"then\": \"connection rejected with 403 Forbidden\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-3\",\n          \"given\": \"server is configured\",\n          \"when\": \"configuration allows external binding\",\n          \"then\": \"warning displayed about security implications\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"@trait-websocket-protocol\",\n      \"title\": \"WebSocket Protocol Patterns\",\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-1\",\n          \"given\": \"WebSocket connection is established\",\n          \"when\": \"client connects\",\n          \"then\": \"server assigns unique connection ID and sends connected event with session_id\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-2\",\n          \"given\": \"client wants notifications\",\n          \"when\": \"subscribe command sent with topics array\",\n          \"then\": \"server tracks subscription and sends ack with request_id\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-3\",\n          \"given\": \"client is subscribed to topic\",\n          \"when\": \"relevant change occurs\",\n          \"then\": \"server broadcasts event with format {msg_id, seq, timestamp, topic, event, data}\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-4\",\n          \"given\": \"WebSocket connection is active\",\n          \"when\": \"30 seconds pass without activity\",\n          \"then\": \"server sends ping frame\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-5\",\n          \"given\": \"ping was sent\",\n          \"when\": \"no pong received within 90 seconds\",\n          \"then\": \"connection is closed with code 1001\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-6\",\n          \"given\": \"server sends events\",\n          \"when\": \"client cannot keep up (backpressure)\",\n          \"then\": \"server pauses non-critical broadcasts until drain event\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-7\",\n          \"given\": \"connection is closing\",\n          \"when\": \"close initiated\",\n          \"then\": \"use code 1000 for clean close, 1001 for timeout, 1011 for error\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-8\",\n          \"given\": \"client reconnects after disconnect\",\n          \"when\": \"new connection established\",\n          \"then\": \"client resets sequence tracking (lastSeqProcessed = -1) since server generates new sequence\"\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"_ulid\": \"01KJDQ1GZVK77Y8CETXW2E56TG\",\n  \"slugs\": [],\n  \"title\": \"Web UI WebSocket connection unreliable - continually disconnects and reconnects. Needs investigation\",\n  \"type\": \"task\",\n  \"description\": \"Web UI WebSocket connection unreliable - continually disconnects and reconnects. Needs investigation into reconnection logic, heartbeat handling, or fallback to polling.\",\n  \"spec_ref\": \"@daemon-server\",\n  \"status\": \"needs_work\",\n  \"blocked_by\": [],\n  \"depends_on\": [],\n  \"context\": [],\n  \"priority\": 3,\n  \"tags\": [],\n  \"vcs_refs\": [],\n  \"session_id\": null,\n  \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T19:33:04.635Z\",\n  \"started_at\": \"2026-03-01T07:29:06.129Z\",\n  \"submitted_at\": \"2026-03-01T07:33:44.791Z\",\n  \"notes\": [\n    {\n      \"_ulid\": \"01KJDQC6EMCTTQFKDBQX9JCG55\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T19:38:54.292Z\",\n      \"author\": \"@claude\",\n      \"content\": \"ENRICHMENT — Standalone context for this task:\\n\\n**What**: The Web UI WebSocket connection continually disconnects and reconnects. The `WebSocketManager` in `packages/web-ui/src/lib/websocket/manager.ts` has exponential backoff reconnection (1s, 2s, 4s... max 30s, max 10 attempts), but users report seeing frequent disconnect/reconnect cycles in the console logs. This suggests either the server is closing connections, the keepalive/heartbeat mechanism is missing, or reconnection resets are happening incorrectly.\\n\\n**Where**:\\n- `packages/web-ui/src/lib/websocket/manager.ts` — The WebSocketManager class. Key areas:\\n  - `connect()` (line 150): creates WebSocket, sets up onopen/onmessage/onerror/onclose handlers\\n  - `scheduleReconnect()` (line 371): exponential backoff logic, max 10 attempts\\n  - `onclose` handler (line 183): triggers reconnect on any close event, even clean ones\\n  - No heartbeat/ping mechanism — if the server expects periodic pings, the connection may time out\\n- `packages/web-ui/src/lib/stores/connection.svelte.ts` — Connection store wrapping the manager\\n- Server-side WebSocket handler (in the daemon code) — check if it sends pings or has idle timeouts\\n\\n**How**: Investigation and fix areas:\\n1. **Add heartbeat/ping**: Implement a periodic ping from client to server (e.g., every 30s). Many WebSocket servers close idle connections after a timeout (often 60s). The client should send a ping command and expect a pong response.\\n2. **Don't reconnect on clean close**: The `onclose` handler (line 183) calls `scheduleReconnect()` unconditionally. If `event.code === 1000` (normal closure) and the client initiated it via `disconnect()`, skip reconnection. Currently `disconnect()` clears the timer, but there's a race if onclose fires after disconnect resets state.\\n3. **Check server-side idle timeout**: The daemon's WebSocket server may have an idle timeout that closes connections. Either increase it or implement heartbeat to keep alive.\\n4. **Consider connection health check**: After reconnecting, verify the connection is actually healthy (e.g., send a ping and wait for response) before transitioning to 'connected' state.\\n5. **Investigate MAX_RECONNECT_ATTEMPTS**: After 10 failed reconnects, the connection is abandoned permanently. Consider resetting the attempt counter after a successful connection that lasts longer than some threshold (e.g., 60s).\\n\\n**Done when**:\\n- WebSocket connection remains stable for extended periods without spurious disconnects\\n- Client sends periodic heartbeat/ping to prevent idle timeout\\n- Clean disconnects (code 1000 from client-initiated disconnect) don't trigger reconnection\\n- Console shows clean connection lifecycle without repeated disconnect/reconnect spam\\n- Connection lost indicator (10s threshold) only triggers for genuine server unavailability\\n- Tests cover: heartbeat keeps connection alive, clean close doesn't reconnect, reconnection works after genuine server restart\",\n      \"supersedes\": null,\n      \"superseded\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"_ulid\": \"01KJDQX0Y1T915X3M23D1VS9PP\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T19:48:05.698Z\",\n      \"author\": \"@claude\",\n      \"content\": \"Linked to @daemon-server spec (covers WebSocket protocol). Investigate and fix WebSocket reconnection reliability.\",\n      \"supersedes\": null,\n      \"superseded\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"_ulid\": \"01KJM2DPN621APMNNFFZCX3RN5\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-03-01T06:47:24.582Z\",\n      \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n      \"content\": \"Execution context:\\n- Background: Web UI websocket manager can enter reconnect churn due to stale onclose handlers from prior sockets and reconnect attempts after intentional disconnect.\\n- Scope: stabilize client connection lifecycle for intentional close and project-switch reconnects; add focused regression tests for stale-close and manual-disconnect behavior.\\n- Files: packages/web-ui/src/lib/websocket/manager.ts, tests/web-ui/websocket-manager.test.ts (new).\\n- Verification: run targeted vitest for websocket manager tests and relevant existing connection-related tests, then run full npm test before submit.\",\n      \"supersedes\": null,\n      \"superseded\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"_ulid\": \"01KJM2R4EQV8T6WJV405GP3XWQ\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-03-01T06:53:06.391Z\",\n      \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n      \"content\": \"Implemented WebSocket reconnect-stability fix in packages/web-ui/src/lib/websocket/manager.ts and added regression tests in tests/websocket-manager.test.ts.\\n\\nWhat changed:\\n- Added stale-socket guards in connect() event handlers so late events from old sockets are ignored and cannot null out the active connection.\\n- Added intentionalDisconnect tracking so manual disconnects do not schedule reconnect attempts.\\n- Updated disconnect() to detach current socket reference before close, preventing close-handler races with new connections.\\n- Added regression tests for:\\n  1) old-socket close after project switch does not disrupt active socket,\\n  2) intentional disconnect does not auto-reconnect,\\n  3) unexpected disconnect still triggers reconnect.\\n\\nVerification:\\n- npx vitest run tests/websocket-manager.test.ts (3 passed)\\n- npm test (fails on pre-existing baseline issues unrelated to this change):\\n  - tests/cli-serve.test.ts \\\"should show No projects registered when no projects exist\\\"\\n  - tests/cli/session-note-limit.test.ts timeout failures (2 cases)\\n- kspec validate (pre-existing project-wide schema/reference/alignment/completeness issues)\",\n      \"supersedes\": null,\n      \"superseded\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"_ulid\": \"01KJM2TCM0Y1NCBBZ9JZTKW183\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-03-01T06:54:20.288Z\",\n      \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n      \"content\": \"Submitted for review in PR #622: https://github.com/kynetic-ai/kynetic-spec/pull/622 (branch fix/web-ui-websocket-reconnect-race, commit 155276ca9). Implemented WebSocketManager stale-close race guard and intentional-disconnect reconnect suppression with regression coverage in tests/websocket-manager.test.ts. Verification: npx vitest run tests/websocket-manager.test.ts (3 passed). Full npm test and kspec validate still show pre-existing unrelated baseline failures/issues (cli-serve no-projects assertion, session-note-limit timeouts, existing validate schema/reference/alignment/completeness warnings/errors).\",\n      \"supersedes\": null,\n      \"superseded\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"_ulid\": \"01KJM385VE2C92BYG0GM4HK06T\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-03-01T07:01:52.110Z\",\n      \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n      \"content\": \"[FIX_CYCLE: 1] Review findings: MUST-FIX: PR #622 failed regression gate. npm test reports 3 failures (tests/cli-serve.test.ts foreground startup assertion; tests/cli/session-note-limit.test.ts two timeout failures). Review posted with inline comment; do not merge until full suite is green.\",\n      \"supersedes\": null,\n      \"superseded\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"_ulid\": \"01KJM52BE1CPS3RB3YKACD24BJ\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-03-01T07:33:38.369Z\",\n      \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n      \"content\": \"[FIX_CYCLE: 2] Rebased branch fix/web-ui-websocket-reconnect-race onto origin/main after PR #621 merged regression-flake fixes. Verified full suite on rebased head: npm test => 163 files passed, 3620 tests passed, 0 failed (3 skipped). No functional changes to websocket fix; update is to clear regression gate with current base.\",\n      \"supersedes\": null,\n      \"superseded\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"_ulid\": \"01KJM53KANY59NF9XDMGZ01TXT\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-03-01T07:34:19.221Z\",\n      \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n      \"content\": \"[FIX_CYCLE: 2] Force-pushed rebased head d0de668 to PR #622 and resolved prior MUST-FIX review thread after confirming full-suite pass. Re-ran check-unresolved-comments workflow to refresh status on the resolved thread.\",\n      \"supersedes\": null,\n      \"superseded\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"_ulid\": \"01KJMTH46XE9XKDEYD1YBBK6D4\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-03-01T13:48:42.590Z\",\n      \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n      \"content\": \"[FIX_CYCLE: 4] Review findings: MUST-FIX: PR #622 fails regression gate on current head d0de668 (CI test shard 2/3). New test tests/websocket-manager.test.ts triggers ReferenceError: crypto is not defined when subscribe() calls crypto.randomUUID(). Address CI compatibility and re-submit for review.\",\n      \"supersedes\": null,\n      \"superseded\": false\n    }\n  ],\n  \"todos\": [],\n  \"automation\": \"eligible\",\n  \"_sourceFile\": \"/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\",\n  \"inherited_traits\": [\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"@trait-json-output\",\n      \"title\": \"JSON Output Mode\",\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-1\",\n          \"given\": \"command supports JSON mode\",\n          \"when\": \"--json flag is provided\",\n          \"then\": \"output is valid JSON with no ANSI color codes\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-2\",\n          \"given\": \"JSON mode is active\",\n          \"when\": \"command completes successfully\",\n          \"then\": \"output includes all data available in human-readable mode\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-3\",\n          \"given\": \"JSON mode is active\",\n          \"when\": \"command encounters an error\",\n          \"then\": \"error is returned as JSON object with error field\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-4\",\n          \"given\": \"JSON output contains references\",\n          \"when\": \"output is generated\",\n          \"then\": \"references use @ prefix consistently\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-5\",\n          \"given\": \"JSON output contains timestamps\",\n          \"when\": \"output is generated\",\n          \"then\": \"timestamps use ISO 8601 format\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-6\",\n          \"given\": \"command supports --json\",\n          \"when\": \"used with other formatting flags\",\n          \"then\": \"--json takes precedence over other format options\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"@trait-error-guidance\",\n      \"title\": \"Error Messages with Recovery Guidance\",\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-1\",\n          \"given\": \"command encounters error\",\n          \"when\": \"error message is shown\",\n          \"then\": \"includes description of what went wrong\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-2\",\n          \"given\": \"command encounters error\",\n          \"when\": \"error message is shown\",\n          \"then\": \"includes suggested action to resolve\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-3\",\n          \"given\": \"reference not found\",\n          \"when\": \"error is shown\",\n          \"then\": \"suggests checking ref with kspec search or kspec <type> list\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-4\",\n          \"given\": \"invalid state transition\",\n          \"when\": \"error is shown\",\n          \"then\": \"indicates current state and valid next states\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-5\",\n          \"given\": \"validation error\",\n          \"when\": \"error is shown\",\n          \"then\": \"indicates which field/value failed validation\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-6\",\n          \"given\": \"error in JSON mode\",\n          \"when\": \"--json is active\",\n          \"then\": \"guidance included in structured error object\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"@trait-shadow-commit\",\n      \"title\": \"Shadow Branch Auto-Commit\",\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-1\",\n          \"given\": \"command modifies state in shadow worktree\",\n          \"when\": \"save operation completes successfully\",\n          \"then\": \"git commit is created in shadow branch with semantic message\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-2\",\n          \"given\": \"shadow commit is created\",\n          \"when\": \"commit message is generated\",\n          \"then\": \"message follows pattern operation-colon-ref-short with optional detail\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-3\",\n          \"given\": \"shadow commit is created\",\n          \"when\": \"item reference is available\",\n          \"then\": \"commit message includes ULID prefix (8 chars) or primary slug\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-4\",\n          \"given\": \"shadow is not configured (no worktree)\",\n          \"when\": \"command that would normally commit runs\",\n          \"then\": \"command completes successfully without attempting git operations\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-5\",\n          \"given\": \"save operation fails\",\n          \"when\": \"validation or IO error occurs\",\n          \"then\": \"no commit is attempted and error is returned\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-6\",\n          \"given\": \"shadow has remote configured\",\n          \"when\": \"commit succeeds\",\n          \"then\": \"push is attempted in fire-and-forget mode (failure doesn't block command)\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-7\",\n          \"given\": \"commit or push fails\",\n          \"when\": \"save succeeded but git operation failed\",\n          \"then\": \"command succeeds but outputs warning about sync state\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-8\",\n          \"given\": \"command performs multiple related saves\",\n          \"when\": \"all saves complete successfully\",\n          \"then\": \"single atomic commit covers all changes\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"@trait-localhost-security\",\n      \"title\": \"Localhost-Only Security\",\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-1\",\n          \"given\": \"server is starting\",\n          \"when\": \"binding to network interface\",\n          \"then\": \"only accepts connections from 127.0.0.1 and ::1 (IPv6 localhost)\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-2\",\n          \"given\": \"connection attempt from non-localhost\",\n          \"when\": \"request received\",\n          \"then\": \"connection rejected with 403 Forbidden\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-3\",\n          \"given\": \"server is configured\",\n          \"when\": \"configuration allows external binding\",\n          \"then\": \"warning displayed about security implications\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"@trait-websocket-protocol\",\n      \"title\": \"WebSocket Protocol Patterns\",\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-1\",\n          \"given\": \"WebSocket connection is established\",\n          \"when\": \"client connects\",\n          \"then\": \"server assigns unique connection ID and sends connected event with session_id\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-2\",\n          \"given\": \"client wants notifications\",\n          \"when\": \"subscribe command sent with topics array\",\n          \"then\": \"server tracks subscription and sends ack with request_id\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-3\",\n          \"given\": \"client is subscribed to topic\",\n          \"when\": \"relevant change occurs\",\n          \"then\": \"server broadcasts event with format {msg_id, seq, timestamp, topic, event, data}\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-4\",\n          \"given\": \"WebSocket connection is active\",\n          \"when\": \"30 seconds pass without activity\",\n          \"then\": \"server sends ping frame\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-5\",\n          \"given\": \"ping was sent\",\n          \"when\": \"no pong received within 90 seconds\",\n          \"then\": \"connection is closed with code 1001\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-6\",\n          \"given\": \"server sends events\",\n          \"when\": \"client cannot keep up (backpressure)\",\n          \"then\": \"server pauses non-critical broadcasts until drain event\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-7\",\n          \"given\": \"connection is closing\",\n          \"when\": \"close initiated\",\n          \"then\": \"use code 1000 for clean close, 1001 for timeout, 1011 for error\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-8\",\n          \"given\": \"client reconnects after disconnect\",\n          \"when\": \"new connection established\",\n          \"then\": \"client resets sequence tracking (lastSeqProcessed = -1) since server generates new sequence\"\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":943222497},"formatted_output":"{\n  \"_ulid\": \"01KJDQ1GZVK77Y8CETXW2E56TG\",\n  \"slugs\": [],\n  \"title\": \"Web UI WebSocket connection unreliable - continually disconnects and reconnects. Needs investigation\",\n  \"type\": \"task\",\n  \"description\": \"Web UI WebSocket connection unreliable - continually disconnects and reconnects. Needs investigation into reconnection logic, heartbeat handling, or fallback to polling.\",\n  \"spec_ref\": \"@daemon-server\",\n  \"status\": \"needs_work\",\n  \"blocked_by\": [],\n  \"depends_on\": [],\n  \"context\": [],\n  \"priority\": 3,\n  \"tags\": [],\n  \"vcs_refs\": [],\n  \"session_id\": null,\n  \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T19:33:04.635Z\",\n  \"started_at\": \"2026-03-01T07:29:06.129Z\",\n  \"submitted_at\": \"2026-03-01T07:33:44.791Z\",\n  \"notes\": [\n    {\n      \"_ulid\": \"01KJDQC6EMCTTQFKDBQX9JCG55\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T19:38:54.292Z\",\n      \"author\": \"@claude\",\n      \"content\": \"ENRICHMENT — Standalone context for this task:\\n\\n**What**: The Web UI WebSocket connection continually disconnects and reconnects. The `WebSocketManager` in `packages/web-ui/src/lib/websocket/manager.ts` has exponential backoff reconnection (1s, 2s, 4s... max 30s, max 10 attempts), but users report seeing frequent disconnect/reconnect cycles in the console logs. This suggests either the server is closing connections, the keepalive/heartbeat mechanism is missing, or reconnection resets are happening incorrectly.\\n\\n**Where**:\\n- `packages/web-ui/src/lib/websocket/manager.ts` — The WebSocketManager class. Key areas:\\n  - `connect()` (line 150): creates WebSocket, sets up onopen/onmessage/onerror/onclose handlers\\n  - `scheduleReconnect()` (line 371): exponential backoff logic, max 10 attempts\\n  - `onclose` handler (line 183): triggers reconnect on any close event, even clean ones\\n  - No heartbeat/ping mechanism — if the server expects periodic pings, the connection may time out\\n- `packages/web-ui/src/lib/stores/connection.svelte.ts` — Connection store wrapping the manager\\n- Server-side WebSocket handler (in the daemon code) — check if it sends pings or has idle timeouts\\n\\n**How**: Investigation and fix areas:\\n1. **Add heartbeat/ping**: Implement a periodic ping from client to server (e.g., every 30s). Many WebSocket servers close idle connections after a timeout (often 60s). The client should send a ping command and expect a pong response.\\n2. **Don't reconnect on clean close**: The `onclose` handler (line 183) calls `scheduleReconnect()` unconditionally. If `event.code === 1000` (normal closure) and the client initiated it via `disconnect()`, skip reconnection. Currently `disconnect()` clears the timer, but there's a race if onclose fires after disconnect resets state.\\n3. **Check server-side idle timeout**: The daemon's WebSocket server may have an idle timeout that closes connections. Either increase it or implement heartbeat to keep alive.\\n4. **Consider connection health check**: After reconnecting, verify the connection is actually healthy (e.g., send a ping and wait for response) before transitioning to 'connected' state.\\n5. **Investigate MAX_RECONNECT_ATTEMPTS**: After 10 failed reconnects, the connection is abandoned permanently. Consider resetting the attempt counter after a successful connection that lasts longer than some threshold (e.g., 60s).\\n\\n**Done when**:\\n- WebSocket connection remains stable for extended periods without spurious disconnects\\n- Client sends periodic heartbeat/ping to prevent idle timeout\\n- Clean disconnects (code 1000 from client-initiated disconnect) don't trigger reconnection\\n- Console shows clean connection lifecycle without repeated disconnect/reconnect spam\\n- Connection lost indicator (10s threshold) only triggers for genuine server unavailability\\n- Tests cover: heartbeat keeps connection alive, clean close doesn't reconnect, reconnection works after genuine server restart\",\n      \"supersedes\": null,\n      \"superseded\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"_ulid\": \"01KJDQX0Y1T915X3M23D1VS9PP\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T19:48:05.698Z\",\n      \"author\": \"@claude\",\n      \"content\": \"Linked to @daemon-server spec (covers WebSocket protocol). Investigate and fix WebSocket reconnection reliability.\",\n      \"supersedes\": null,\n      \"superseded\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"_ulid\": \"01KJM2DPN621APMNNFFZCX3RN5\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-03-01T06:47:24.582Z\",\n      \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n      \"content\": \"Execution context:\\n- Background: Web UI websocket manager can enter reconnect churn due to stale onclose handlers from prior sockets and reconnect attempts after intentional disconnect.\\n- Scope: stabilize client connection lifecycle for intentional close and project-switch reconnects; add focused regression tests for stale-close and manual-disconnect behavior.\\n- Files: packages/web-ui/src/lib/websocket/manager.ts, tests/web-ui/websocket-manager.test.ts (new).\\n- Verification: run targeted vitest for websocket manager tests and relevant existing connection-related tests, then run full npm test before submit.\",\n      \"supersedes\": null,\n      \"superseded\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"_ulid\": \"01KJM2R4EQV8T6WJV405GP3XWQ\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-03-01T06:53:06.391Z\",\n      \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n      \"content\": \"Implemented WebSocket reconnect-stability fix in packages/web-ui/src/lib/websocket/manager.ts and added regression tests in tests/websocket-manager.test.ts.\\n\\nWhat changed:\\n- Added stale-socket guards in connect() event handlers so late events from old sockets are ignored and cannot null out the active connection.\\n- Added intentionalDisconnect tracking so manual disconnects do not schedule reconnect attempts.\\n- Updated disconnect() to detach current socket reference before close, preventing close-handler races with new connections.\\n- Added regression tests for:\\n  1) old-socket close after project switch does not disrupt active socket,\\n  2) intentional disconnect does not auto-reconnect,\\n  3) unexpected disconnect still triggers reconnect.\\n\\nVerification:\\n- npx vitest run tests/websocket-manager.test.ts (3 passed)\\n- npm test (fails on pre-existing baseline issues unrelated to this change):\\n  - tests/cli-serve.test.ts \\\"should show No projects registered when no projects exist\\\"\\n  - tests/cli/session-note-limit.test.ts timeout failures (2 cases)\\n- kspec validate (pre-existing project-wide schema/reference/alignment/completeness issues)\",\n      \"supersedes\": null,\n      \"superseded\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"_ulid\": \"01KJM2TCM0Y1NCBBZ9JZTKW183\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-03-01T06:54:20.288Z\",\n      \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n      \"content\": \"Submitted for review in PR #622: https://github.com/kynetic-ai/kynetic-spec/pull/622 (branch fix/web-ui-websocket-reconnect-race, commit 155276ca9). Implemented WebSocketManager stale-close race guard and intentional-disconnect reconnect suppression with regression coverage in tests/websocket-manager.test.ts. Verification: npx vitest run tests/websocket-manager.test.ts (3 passed). Full npm test and kspec validate still show pre-existing unrelated baseline failures/issues (cli-serve no-projects assertion, session-note-limit timeouts, existing validate schema/reference/alignment/completeness warnings/errors).\",\n      \"supersedes\": null,\n      \"superseded\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"_ulid\": \"01KJM385VE2C92BYG0GM4HK06T\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-03-01T07:01:52.110Z\",\n      \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n      \"content\": \"[FIX_CYCLE: 1] Review findings: MUST-FIX: PR #622 failed regression gate. npm test reports 3 failures (tests/cli-serve.test.ts foreground startup assertion; tests/cli/session-note-limit.test.ts two timeout failures). Review posted with inline comment; do not merge until full suite is green.\",\n      \"supersedes\": null,\n      \"superseded\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"_ulid\": \"01KJM52BE1CPS3RB3YKACD24BJ\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-03-01T07:33:38.369Z\",\n      \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n      \"content\": \"[FIX_CYCLE: 2] Rebased branch fix/web-ui-websocket-reconnect-race onto origin/main after PR #621 merged regression-flake fixes. Verified full suite on rebased head: npm test => 163 files passed, 3620 tests passed, 0 failed (3 skipped). No functional changes to websocket fix; update is to clear regression gate with current base.\",\n      \"supersedes\": null,\n      \"superseded\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"_ulid\": \"01KJM53KANY59NF9XDMGZ01TXT\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-03-01T07:34:19.221Z\",\n      \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n      \"content\": \"[FIX_CYCLE: 2] Force-pushed rebased head d0de668 to PR #622 and resolved prior MUST-FIX review thread after confirming full-suite pass. Re-ran check-unresolved-comments workflow to refresh status on the resolved thread.\",\n      \"supersedes\": null,\n      \"superseded\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"_ulid\": \"01KJMTH46XE9XKDEYD1YBBK6D4\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-03-01T13:48:42.590Z\",\n      \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n      \"content\": \"[FIX_CYCLE: 4] Review findings: MUST-FIX: PR #622 fails regression gate on current head d0de668 (CI test shard 2/3). New test tests/websocket-manager.test.ts triggers ReferenceError: crypto is not defined when subscribe() calls crypto.randomUUID(). Address CI compatibility and re-submit for review.\",\n      \"supersedes\": null,\n      \"superseded\": false\n    }\n  ],\n  \"todos\": [],\n  \"automation\": \"eligible\",\n  \"_sourceFile\": \"/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\",\n  \"inherited_traits\": [\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"@trait-json-outpu